    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the build is green (2/2 tests pass, and this is the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nI converted owner deletion to a soft-delete. The changes:\n\n**Model & schema**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `deleted` field (`Boolean`, defaulting to `false`) with getter/setter and a `deleted` column mapping.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` (used by tests) plus `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` schemas \u2014 added a `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` column. The hsqldb `data.sql` uses positional inserts, so I appended `FALSE` to each seed owner row; the other DBs use column-list inserts and rely on the default.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\n**Behavior**\n- `function/owner/DeleteOwner.java` \u2014 now sets `deleted = true` and saves the owner instead of removing the row, so `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` retains the record and returns 204 (2xx). `GET` afterward still returns the owner with `deleted: true`.\n- `function/owner/RequireUniqueIdentity.java` \u2014 skips soft-deleted owners, so a normally-blocking duplicate/identity match is allowed when the only match is deleted.\n- `function/owner/FlagPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 also skips soft-deleted owners in the soft-match duplicate check, keeping the \"ignore deleted\" behavior consistent.\n\nA newly created owner reports `deleted: false` (entity default, persisted); after DELETE it reports `deleted: true`; and re-creating a previously-deleted owner now succeeds. Both new acceptance tests (`coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`, `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`) pass, and the full suite is green.",
